        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Béla Bartók, Dmitri Shostakovich, Vyacheslav Nagovitsin\n- Roles: composers, pianists, ethnomusicologists, student\n- Organizations: Leningrad Conservatory\n\nFacts:\n- Béla Bartók was born on 25 March 1881 and died on 26 September 1945.\n- Béla Bartók was a Hungarian composer, pianist, and ethnomusicologist.\n- Dmitri Shostakovich was born on 25 September 1906 and died on 9 August 1975.\n- Dmitri Shostakovich was a Russian composer and pianist.\n- Vyacheslav Nagovitsin studied under Dmitri Shostakovich at the Leningrad Conservatory.\n- Vyacheslav Nagovitsin graduated from the undergraduate school of the Leningrad Conservatory in 1963.\n- Vyacheslav Nagovitsin graduated from postgraduate school at the Leningrad Conservatory in 1966.",
